# SmartFlow NLEX - frontend environment
#
# Unlike the backend, this app's .env IS committed on purpose: every key here
# is NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which means it is compiled into the browser bundle and is
# public the moment the site ships. Nothing secret can live in this file.
#
# IMPORTANT - this app builds with `output: 'export'` (a static export), so
# these values are BAKED IN AT BUILD TIME, not read at runtime. Changing the
# backend URL means rebuilding and redeploying; editing an env var in the
# Vercel console after the fact changes nothing until the next build.

# Where the Express backend lives.
#   local    http://localhost:4000
#   prod     the Railway public URL
# A build made with the local value ships a site that asks every visitor's own
# machine for data, which fails for everyone but you. Set this before building
# for production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=

# Mapbox GL token. Public by design, so restrict it by URL in the Mapbox
# console to the deployed domain - otherwise anyone can spend your quota.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# Supabase project that issues operator session tokens.
# The anon key is public by Supabase's design: it ships in the browser bundle
# and is protected by row-level security, not secrecy. Safe in this file and
# in the committed .env; the SERVICE ROLE key never is, and is not used here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
